<title>SPAIN: Spain to put 4 pct tax on nonlife, social insurance.</title>
<headline>Spain to put 4 pct tax on nonlife, social insurance.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's government proposed on Friday the levying a four percent tax on non-life and social insurance in 1997, Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato told journalists.</p>
<p>&quot;The government is considering a four percent tax,&quot; Rato said, speaking to journalists following a cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>The bill will accompany the 1997 budget but is not expected to be approved until October.</p>
<p>Social insurance could include coverage for dismissal or accident.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
